# 20-era5c-dev-hooks.patch: era-5c's owner patch against borrow-ownership@b0eb75189, applied by the AE
# derivation's step 2 after 10- (`git apply`, name order; crat-packaging 025 §4, relay era-5c/258, R1281-3).
# Every file it touches is under crates/pointer_replacer/src/analyses/borrow_ownership/; it shares no file with 10-
# and applies to b0eb75189 alone or after 10-.
#
# Rows of docs/agents/artifacts/2026-10-22-crat-packaging-025/d-rows.tsv, lane era-5c (122), and how each closes:
#   dev switch (16)    The reader and every branch it gates are removed; each branch only printed to stderr or wrote
#                      a dump file. CRAT_ERA5C_DEBUG (31 reads, one in the cache key), CRAT_E5C_CR_STATS
#                      (with the per-reason counts that fed it), CRAT_E5C_MERGE_STATS, CRAT_E5C_READER_DEBUG,
#                      CRAT_E5C_SINK_DEBUG, CRAT_ERA5C_BYTEPROOF (with the test-only CRAT_ERA5_BYTE_PROOF),
#                      CRAT_ERA5C_EQ_BACKTRACE, CRAT_ERA5C_FIELDSIZE,
#                      CRAT_ERA5C_RESEAT_DUMP, CRAT_ERA5C_RESEAT_WHY, CRAT_R377_DEBUG, CRAT_R388_DEBUG,
#                      CRAT_BO_REQUIRER_DROP_OUT (its sink, the attribution it fed and the closure it alone computed),
#                      CRAT_POINTER_DECISION_DIAGNOSTICS and CRAT_BO_L2_TRANSITION_DIAGNOSTICS (the [bo-l2] prints,
#                      the flag's plumbing, L2TransitionDiagnostics). CRAT_BO_EXPORT leaves the cache key; its parse
#                      is compiler-dead (step 6).
#   test hook (12)     CRAT_E5C_W47_FAULT / W49 / W52 leave the cache key, with their #[cfg(test)] readers. The
#                      cfg!(test) sites fold to their no-fault arm: W71 (eight sites), W76, W80, W81 (two), W84,
#                      W85 (two); the READER / SINK / LEDGER_ALSO prints go with their switches.
#                      esc_minimal's fixture_selection_enabled() (false outside tests) folds into select().
#                      CRAT_E5C_W79_FAULT (analyses/borrow/mod.rs) is closed by 10-.
#   measurement (12)   The raw-cause ledger goes whole: raw_cause.rs, its five names (CRAT_ERA5C_RAW_CAUSE_LEDGER,
#                      _BUDGET_S, _LABELS, CRAT_ERA5C_EAGER_DUMP, CRAT_E5C_LEDGER_ALSO), its call sites, the
#                      replay's recording arm and the eager-exclusion notes; the non-recording arms stay, which is
#                      what runs with the ledger off (the artifact's run.sh sets it off for every translate).
#                      The job identity is no longer read: CRAT_ERA5_LAUNCH_DIGEST, CRAT_ERA5_PROGRAM,
#                      CRAT_ERA5_INPUT_ROOT, CRAT_ERA5_TOOLCHAIN_DIGEST, CRAT_ERA5_DEPENDENCY_DIGEST. The cache key
#                      takes the crate name, the sources' common root and the sha256 of rust-toolchain.toml and
#                      Cargo.lock: the values it computed when those were unset.
#                      CRAT_ERA5_EXECUTION_ROLE is no longer read: the role is Derive unless a scope sets it, the
#                      same as `derive` or unset.
#                      solver_identity loses its constant fields: WORKER_HOSTS, ANALYSIS_FRAME, the four markers
#                      (positive-opacity-v1, modeled-origin-one-way-v1, endpoint-force-retraction-v1,
#                      direct-escape-minimal-v1), the allowlist digest, the schema, the query timeout and the ten
#                      fixed rule labels. The analyses-tree hash in the key already covers code and data files.
#   measurement (kit)  config/analysis-env.sh l.51 JOBCRAT_ERA5_EXECUTION_ROLE=derive: no reader after this patch.
#                      CONFIG_DROP can take it, with _TOOLCHAIN_DIGEST, _DEPENDENCY_DIGEST,
#                      _RAW_CAUSE_LEDGER and _RAW_CAUSE_BUDGET_S, which also have no reader now.
#   dead code (81)     Compiler-listed items go by step 6's deadcut. This patch cuts only those that read a field
#                      or variant it removes, plus the three deadcut leaves (PlaceKey::derefs / fields; the trait
#                      methods AnalysisKind::analyze and FnResults::local_result, with their impls).
#                      Never-read fields (11 rows) go with their initializers, every one side-effect free (getters,
#                      clones, pure renders, timers). Of these structs only reader_replay::Failure has its derived
#                      Debug formatted anywhere: a cargo check with Debug stripped from all of them fails only on
#                      borrow_verify's replay assert message, so Failure's three fields stay.
#                      StreamHashes' payload / exports stay: their one reader is the compiler-dead
#                      bo_rewriter/decision/ownership_fields_cache_binding.rs::bind (another lane's file, step 6's).
#                      Fields left unread by these cuts went too (A5Plan's site ledger, BoConstruction's stats and
#                      timers, esc_minimal's Pending::source). EscMinimalSelection's site lists become counts.
#                      Never-constructed variants (13 groups) go with their match arms. None of their enums derives
#                      Hash, and ReturnPortHold (Ord) loses its last variant only.
#
# Not in this patch:
#   - solver_identity's fields that name a switch the tree still reads (the B rows, the user's): while a switch
#     exists, the key must separate its arms;
#   - the compiler-listed dead items no field cut needed (step 6), and the field / variant warnings left by them;
#   - the test build of the patched head: tests that read a removed item no longer compile, and the fixture
#     selection's test scope is now inert; step 4 cuts cfg(test) before any build.
#
# Output: unchanged by construction. Each removed branch was gated by a variable the artifact never sets, or by
# cfg(test), or the code was unreachable; the variables the artifact does set (EXECUTION_ROLE=derive, the two
# recipe digests, RAW_CAUSE_LEDGER, which run.sh overrides to off) now take the value or arm they had.
# CRAT_ERA5_PROGRAM, which b0eb75189's run.sh set per program (the kit's run.sh no longer does), fed only the
# cache key's program label here. The cache key changes value, but it still separates every switch the tree reads
# and the A5 mode and attestation; the artifact configures no model cache.
# Checks on the patched b0eb75189 (10- then 20-): `git apply --check` on a clean b0eb75189 (alone and after
# 10-); `cargo fmt --check -p pointer_replacer` clean; `cargo check -p pointer_replacer` rc 0 and
# `cargo build --release --bin crat` rc 0; on b0eb75189 + 20- alone, `cargo check` rc 0.
# Warnings, by file and message: 633 -> 633 with the tree's allow lines (630 -> 630 without 10-); with
# borrow_ownership's dead-code allows out, 258 -> 222 there (field groups 18 -> 2, the two kept above; variant groups
# 11 -> 0; the rest compiler-dead items for step 6, 14 of them named items whose last reader this patch removes,
# e.g. parse_role, a5_mark_artifact, origin evidence's canonical_json).
